===================== Habitat navigation (IMR lab) =====================

terminal 1  (build once, and after every code change)

conda activate habitat
cd ~/robo_project_ws
rm -rf build install log
colcon build
source install/setup.bash

terminal 2  (Habitat simulator bridge: cameras, /odom, TF; drives with /cmd_vel)

conda activate habitat
cd ~/robo_project_ws
source install/setup.bash
python3 src/robo_project/habitat_bridge_vinebot_2.py
#   other scene:  python3 src/robo_project/habitat_bridge_vinebot_2.py --ros-args -p scene_path:=/path/to/scene.glb

terminal 3  (robot model for RViz)

cd ~/robo_project_ws
source install/setup.bash
ros2 launch vinebot_description robot_launch.py

terminal 4  (RViz; use "2D Goal Pose" to send the robot somewhere)

conda activate habitat
cd ~/robo_project_ws
source install/setup.bash
rviz2 -d src/vinebot_description/config/display_vinebot.rviz

terminal 5  (map server + A* motion planner + path-following runner)

conda activate habitat
cd ~/robo_project_ws
source install/setup.bash
ros2 launch robo_project run.launch.py
#   initial goal:  ros2 launch robo_project run.launch.py goal_x:=1.0 goal_y:=-2.0

Notes
- The map comes from src/robo_project/config/config.yaml -> map.fname (default: the lab sketch).
- Another config:  export ROBO_PROJECT_CONFIG=config_delton.yaml   (before launching)


===================== Particle-filter validation (dataset replay) =====================

cd ~/robo_project_ws
source install/setup.bash
export ROBO_PROJECT_CONFIG=config_delton.yaml
ros2 launch robo_project pf_validation.launch.py dataset_path:=$HOME/robo_project_ws/dataset/cmn_dataset_delton


